      "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.11.04.10.27.00/linqbuilder.ef6.automapper.1.0.1.json#deprecation/alternatePackage",
      "id": "LinqBuilder.EF6",
      "range": "*"
    },
    "message": "Discontinued in LinqBuilder v2.0.0. Its methods projected the query with AutoMapper before applying the specification, which you can do directly: install LinqBuilder.EF6 and write query.ProjectTo<T>(configuration).AnyAsync(specification), and the same for AllAsync, CountAsync, FirstAsync and the rest. If you rely on computed properties, add .DecompileAsync() from DelegateDecompiler.EntityFramework after ProjectTo, as this package did. Release notes: https://github.com/Baune8D/LinqBuilder/releases/tag/v2.0.0",
    "reasons": [
      "Legacy"
    ]
  },
  "description": "Extensions for querying EF 6 with AutoMapper projections.",
